    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d642">

                <pb facs="0662" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/6–2249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister-Counselor of
                        Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Canton</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-22T19:00:00-04:00">June 22, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>TelCan 369. Clark authorized negotiate extension JCRR agreement in consultation
                    with Moyer accordance Ecato 257 June 21.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d642-f1"/> Dept
                    and ECA suggest fol draft note to Chi Govt:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“I have the honor to refer to the agreement between our two Govts constituted
                        by the exchange of notes dated August 5<anchor n="30" xml:id="d642-f2"/>
                        providing for the establishment of a Sino-American Joint Commission on Rural
                        Reconstruction in China.</p>
                    <p>My Govt proposes that the agreement be extended until the date of termination
                        of the Economic Aid Agreement between our two Govts concluded July 3, 1948,
                        and that references in the exchange of notes to Section 407 of the China Aid
                        Act of 1948 be deemed to include reference to Section 12 of Public Law 47,
                        81st Congress.</p>
                    <p>This note and Your Excellency’s reply accepting the above proposal will
                        constitute an agreement between our two Govts.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
